From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Corrales <deathcamel58@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:33:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-mipi-dsi: count non-burst lbcc in the real
 lane rate

Commit ac87d23694f4 ("drm/bridge: synopsys: dw-mipi-dsi: Use pixel clock
rate to calculate lbcc") computes the horizontal timings of a non-burst
video mode as hcomponent * bpp / (lanes * 8) lane byte clock cycles. That
is exact when the lanes carry the pixel bandwidth and nothing more, as on
the i.MX93 it was written for. Rockchip's PHY setup runs the lanes 25%
faster than that, so on RK3288 every horizontal period comes out about a
fifth short of the line the VOP sends.

The inMusic SC6000 panel (HX8260, VIDEO | SYNC_PULSE, 800x1280 at
73 MHz, lanes at ~548 Mbps) shows only noise fading to white on 6.18,
where 6.6, which counted in lane_mbps, drove it correctly.

Count in the lane byte clock whenever the lanes run faster than the
pixel bandwidth (with a 1 Mbps per lane allowance for lane_mbps being
rounded up), and keep the pixel-clock form for the exact case.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c | 22 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c
index a77ade14141f..06f21d1e4089 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c
@@ -783,17 +783,25 @@ static u32 dw_mipi_dsi_get_hcomponent_lbcc(struct dw_mipi_dsi *dsi,
 	u32 frac, lbcc, minimum_lbcc;
 	int bpp;
 
-	if (dsi->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST) {
+	bpp = mipi_dsi_pixel_format_to_bpp(dsi->format);
+	if (bpp < 0) {
+		dev_err(dsi->dev, "failed to get bpp\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The pixel-clock form is exact only when the lanes carry the pixel
+	 * bandwidth and nothing more. Platforms that run the lanes faster -
+	 * Rockchip adds 25% - must count in the real lane byte clock, or every
+	 * horizontal period comes out short and a non-burst panel loses sync.
+	 */
+	if ((dsi->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST) ||
+	    (u64)dsi->lane_mbps * MSEC_PER_SEC * dsi->lanes >
+	    (u64)mode->clock * bpp + dsi->lanes * MSEC_PER_SEC) {
 		/* lbcc based on lane_mbps */
 		lbcc = hcomponent * dsi->lane_mbps * MSEC_PER_SEC / 8;
 	} else {
 		/* lbcc based on pixel clock rate */
-		bpp = mipi_dsi_pixel_format_to_bpp(dsi->format);
-		if (bpp < 0) {
-			dev_err(dsi->dev, "failed to get bpp\n");
-			return 0;
-		}
-
 		lbcc = div_u64((u64)hcomponent * mode->clock * bpp, dsi->lanes * 8);
 	}
 
